hadiths[114]{hadithnumber,text}:
"4557","Whenever we gave the Pledge of allegiance to Messenger of Allah ﷺ for to listen to and obey, he used to say to us, for as much as you can."" (Using translation from Bukhārī 7202)"
"4558","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) sent Sayyiduna Alqamah bin Mujazzar Mudlaji (may Allah be pleased with him) on an expedition, in"
"4559","Sayyiduna Fadala bin Ubaidullah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates this statement of the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): \""There are three people about whom no question will be asked: one is the person who separates himself from the (Muslim) community and disobeys his ruler, and dies in a state of disobedience; one is the slave-girl who runs away from her master and dies in that state; and one is the woman whose husband is not present, the husband fulfills her worldly needs, and sh"
"4560","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “I command you to do three things and I forbid you from three things. I command you to worship Allah and not associate anything with Him, all of you hold firmly to the rope of Allah and do not become divided, and obey the one whom Allah has appointed as your leader (i.e., the ruler of the time). And I forbid you from useless arguments, excessive (unnecessary) questioning, and was"
"4561","Whenever we gave the Pledge of allegiance to Messenger of Allah ﷺ for to listen to and obey, he used to say to us, for as much as you can."" (Using translation from Bukhārī 7202)"
"4562","Sayyiduna ‘Ubada bin Samit (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates this statement of the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): \""Obey (the ruler of the time) in hardship and ease, in what you like and dislike, and even if he gives preference to others over you (in all circumstances, obey him); if he takes your wealth and strikes your back (still obey him), except if he commands something sinful, then do not obey him in that.\"""""""
"4563","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) was delivering a se"
"4564","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) had placed his sheet on his left shoulder, and it was passing under his right armpit. The narrator says: I saw a raised mark under the bulge of his right shoulder (perhaps this refers to the Seal of Prophethood). (The narrator says) Then the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) spoke at length. Among the things the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said was this: “If a black slave is appointed over you as your leader, whose nose and ears are cut off, and he leads you according to the Book of Allah, then obey and follow him.” Then the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) asked: Have I conveyed (the message)?"
"4565","""We used to pledge to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to hear and obey."" So he would say to us: ""As much as you are able."" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 1593)"
"4566","I replied: I am present. The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Obey (your leaders) in hardship and ease, in things you like and dislike, and even if they take your wealth and strike your back, except when they openly commit disobedience to Allah (then do not obey them)."
"4567","Enter it. Some people wanted to enter it, but others said: This is what we wanted to flee from. That was mentioned to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and he said to those who had wanted to enter it: “If you had entered it you would have remained in it until the Day of Resurrection.” He said some kind words to the others, then he said: ʿThere is no obedience in that which involves disobedience towards Allah; obedience is only with regard to that which is right and proper.ʿ (Using translation from Aḥmad 724)"
"4568","ʿThere is no obedience to any human being if it involves disobedience to Allah.ʿ (Using translation from Aḥmad 1065)"
"4569","ʿThere is no obedience to any human being if it involves disobedience to Allah.ʿ (Using translation from Aḥmad 1065)"
"4570","I only fear for my Ummah from misguided rulers. When the sword is placed among my Ummah (that is, when fighting begins among them), it will not be lifted from them until the Day of Resurrection (that is, their mutual fighting will not end)."
"4571","the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Allah will not take away knowledge by removing it from people (from their hearts). Rather He will take away knowledge by taking away the scholars, then when there are no scholars left, the people will take the ignorant as their leaders. They will be asked questions and they will issue verdicts without knowledge, thus they will go astray and lead others astray.'"" (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 52)"
"4572","I consider you the most intelligent person among the people of Madinah."" (The narrator says) Then the Prophet (peace be upon him) mentioned the Christians and Jews, how they went astray despite having the Book of Allah. The narrator says: Then I met Sayyiduna Shaddad bin Aws (may Allah be pleased with him) and I narrated to him the hadith transmitted by Sayyiduna Awf bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him), so he said: ""Awf (may Allah be pleased with him) has narrated correctly."" Then he said: ""Shall I not tell you which knowledge will be taken away first?"" I said: ""Yes."" He said: ""Taqwa (piety), until you will not see any pious person."
"4573","The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever dies in such a state that he has no Imam (i.e., he is not obedient to any Muslim ruler), then such a person dies the death of the days of ignorance (Jahiliyyah)."" (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) The statement of the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), ""he dies the death of the days of ignorance,"" means: Whoever passes away in such a state that he does not believe that he has an Imam who calls people to the obedience of Allah Almighty and protects the foundations of Islam in times of incidents and difficulties, and that person follows him—if he does not have the qualities we have described, then such a person dies the death of the days of ignorance. (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) Apparently, from this narration, it is understood that whoever passes away in such a state that he has no Imam, by this the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) means: such a person dies the death of the days of ignorance. The reason for this is: The Imam of the people of the earth is the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him). Whoever does not know of the Imamate of the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), he believes in some other Imam besides the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) and gives preference to his statement over the statement of the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), and then dies in that state—such a person dies the death of the days of ignorance."
"4574","""The Messenger of Allah said: 'Religion is sincerity (An-Nasihah).' They said: 'To whom, O Messenger of Allah? He said: 'To Allah, to His Book, to His Messenger, to the imams of the Muslims and to their common folk""' (Using translation from Nasāʾī 4198)"
"4575","The people asked: ""O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)! For whom?"" The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) replied: ""For Allah, His Book, His Messenger, the leaders of the Muslims, and their common people (to be sincere to them)."
"4576","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood before us as I am standing before you, and said: ʿI urge you to show respect to my Companions, then those who come after them, then those who come after them, then lying will become so widespread that a man will start to give testimony before he is asked to do so.Whoever among you wants to attain a spacious abode in Paradise, let him adhere to the jama'ah (main body of Muslims), for the Shaitan is with the one who is alone, but he is further away from two. And no one of you should be alone with a woman for the Shaitan will be the third one present. The one who is pleased with his good deeds and upset by his bad deeds is a believer.ʿ (Using translation from Aḥmad 114)"
"4577","""I saw the Prophet [SAW] on the Minbar addressing the people. He said: 'After me there will be many calamities and much evil behavior. Whoever you see splitting away from the Jama'ah or trying to create division among the Ummah of Muhammad [SAW], then kill him, for the Hand of Allah is with the Jama'ah, and the Shaitan is with the one who splits away from the Ummah, running with him.'"" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 4020)"
"4578","I have not come here to sit; I have come to say two things to you which I heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him). I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: “Whoever withdraws his hand from obedience (to the ruler), he will have no proof for himself on the Day of Resurrection, and whoever dies having separated from the congregation (of Muslims), he dies the death of ignorance (Jahiliyyah).”"
"4579","The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever is killed under a banner of misguidance dies the death of the days of ignorance (Jahiliyyah)."
"4580","One who defected from obedience (to the Amir) and separated from the main body of the Muslims - if he died in that state-would die the death of one belonging to the days of Jahiliyya (i.e. would not die as a Muslim). One who fights under the banner of a people who are blind (to the cause for which they are fighting, i.e. do not know whether their cause is just or otherwise), who gets flared up with family pride, calls (people) to fight for their family honour, and supports his kith and kin (i.e. fights not for the cause of Allah but for the sake of this family or tribe) - if he is killed (in this fight), he dies as one belonging to the days of Jahiliyya. Whoso attacks my Ummah (indiscriminately) killing the righteous and the wicked of them, sparing not (even) those staunch in faith and fulfilling not his promise made with those who have been given a pledge of security - he has nothing to do with me and I have nothing to do with him. (Using translation from Muslim 1848a)"
"4581","I have a right over the Quraysh, and the Quraysh have a right over you people. When they judge, let them do so with justice; when they are entrusted with something, let them fulfill the trust; and when mercy is sought from them, let them show mercy. Whoever does not do so, the curse of Allah shall be upon him."
"4582","I will stand in front of them."
"4583","The chief of Quraysh) ‘Urwah was present with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). While talking to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), ‘Urwah extended his hand towards the Prophet’s beard. Sayyiduna Mughirah (may Allah be pleased with him) said to ‘Urwah: Either you withdraw your hand from the beard of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), or it will not return to you safely. ‘Urwah asked: Who is this person? It was said: This is your nephew, Mughirah bin Shu’bah. So ‘Urwah said: O betrayer! You have not yet washed your head after your betrayal."
"4584","I have a right over the Quraysh and the Quraysh have a right over you people as long as they judge with justice when making decisions, fulfill the trust when entrusted with it, and show mercy when mercy is sought from them."
"4585","The boy presented his tablet before him. Sayyiduna ‘Amir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: I used to understand some of their speech. When he passed by a verse, I laughed. Najashi asked: What made you laugh? By the One in Whose hand is my soul, this statement has been revealed from the Lord of the Throne. Sayyiduna ‘Isa bin Maryam (peace be upon him) said this: There is a curse upon the land where children rule. (Sayyiduna ‘Amir, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates) I heard this statement from the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him): I heard him say: “Obey the Quraysh and leave their personal actions (to their own state).”"
"4586","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Soon there will come rulers over you who will make the worst people among the people their close associates. They will delay the prayer from its prescribed time. Whoever among you lives in their time, let him not become a government official, soldier, employee, or treasurer."
"4587","The Prophet ﷺ said, ""Soon others will be preferred to you, and there will be things which you will not like."" The companions of the Prophet ﷺ asked, ""O Messenger of Allah ﷺ! What do you order us to do (in this case)? "" He said, ""(I order you) to give the rights that are on you and to ask your rights from Allah."" (Using translation from Bukhārī 3603)"
"4588","“Whoever bears weapons against us is not one of us.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 2575)"
"4589","The best of your rulers are those whom you love and who love you, who invoke God's blessings upon you and you invoke His blessings upon them. And the worst of your rulers are those whom you hate and who hate you and whom you curse and who curse you. It was asked (by those present): Shouldn't we overthrow them with the help of the sword? He said: No, as long as they establish prayer among you. If you then find anything detestable in them. You should hate their administration, but do not withdraw yourselves from their obedience. (Using translation from Muslim 1855a)"
"4590","“Whoever bears weapons against us is not one of us.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 2575)"
"4591","I was present near the pulpit of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) when a man said: I do not care if, after accepting Islam, I do no other deed except that I populate the Sacred Mosque, or go for Hajj or ‘Umrah to the House of Allah. Another person said: Striving in the path of Allah is more virtuous than what you have mentioned. So Allah Almighty revealed this verse: “Do you consider the providing of water to the pilgrims and the maintenance of al-Masjid al-Haram as equal to the one who believes in Allah and the Last Day and strives in the way of Allah? They are not equal in the sight of Allah. And Allah does not guide the wrongdoing people.”"
"4592","narrates this statement of the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him): ""After the conquest of (Makkah), migration no longer remains, but only jihad and intention (remain)."
"4593","""I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'the Shaitan sits in the paths of the son of Adam. He sits waiting for him, in the path to Islam, and he says: Will you accept Islam, and leave your religion, and the religion of your forefathers? But he disobeys him and accepts Islam. Then he sits waiting for him, on the path to emigration, and he says: Will you emigrate and leave behind your land and sky? The one who emigrates is like a horse tethered to a peg. But he disobeys him and emigrates. Then he sits, waiting for him, on the path to Jihad, and he says: Will you fight in Jihad when it will cost you your life and your wealth? You will fight and be killed, and your wife will remarry, and your wealth will be divided. But he disobeys him and fights in Jihad.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Whoever does that, then he had a right from Allah, the Mighty and Sublime, that He will admit him to paradise. Whoever is killed, he has a right from Allah, the Mighty and Sublime, that He will admit him to Paradise. If he is drowned, he has a right from Allah that He will admit him to paradise, or whoever is thrown by his mount and his neck is broken, he had a right from Allah that he will admit him to Paradise.'"" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 3134)"
"4594","The narrator says: We became apprehensive about any one of us asking the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him). The narrator says: Then the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) called us one by one; he called only us, and we gathered in the presence of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him). Then one of us gestured to another and asked: Why has the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) called us? We feared that perhaps (some command of the Qur'an) had been revealed about us. The narrator says: Then the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) recited this verse before us: ""Whatever is in the heavens and whatever is on the earth glorifies Allah, and He is the Mighty, the Wise. O you who believe! Why do you say what you do not do?"" The narrator says: The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) recited this Surah from the beginning to the end before us. (The narrator says) Then the narrator named Yahya, while narrating this tradition, also recited this Surah from the beginning to the end. Then the narrator named Awza'i also recited this Surah from the beginning to the end. Then the narrator named Walid also recited this Surah from the beginning to the end."
"4595","I bear witness that there is no deity except Allah, and indeed Muhammad (peace be upon him) is the Messenger of Allah."" So the Prophet (peace be upon him) said: ""I also bear witness to this, and I also bear witness that whoever bears witness to this will be free from shirk."
"4596","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""To have faith in Allah, and to strive in His path."" The narrator states: I asked, ""Which slave is the most virtuous?"" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The one who is best in the sight of his master and whose price is the highest."" Sayyiduna Abu Dharr (may Allah be pleased with him) asked: ""If I am not able to do that?"" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Then help someone who is working, or do some work for someone who is unable to do it."" I asked: ""If I am not able to do even that?"" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Then refrain from evil, for this will be a charity that you do for yourself."
"4597","The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The best deed in the sight of Allah Almighty is such faith in which there is no doubt, and such jihad in which there is no dishonesty, and an accepted Hajj."" Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) says: An accepted Hajj wipes out the sins of a whole year. (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) The narrator named Abu Ja'far is Imam Muhammad bin Ali bin Husayn bin Ali bin Abi Talib (that is, Imam Muhammad al-Baqir)."
"4598","""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked: 'Which deed is the most virtuos ? And which deed is the best ?' He ﷺ said: 'Faith in Allah and His Messenger.' It was said: 'Then what ?' He said: 'Jihad is the hump (the most prominent) of the deeds.' Then what O Messenger of Allah ? He said: 'Then Hajj Mabrur.'"" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 1658)"
"4599","“Which of the people is best?” He said: “A man who strives in Jihad in the cause of Allah with himself and his wealth.” He said: “Then who?” He said: “A man in a mountain pass who worships Allah and leaves the people from his evil.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 3978)"
"4600","The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A time will come upon the people when the best person among them in terms of status and rank will be the one who, holding the reins of his horse, sets out in the path of Allah for jihad. Whenever he hears the call to battle, he will mount his horse and seek death (martyrdom), or the person who resides in a mountain pass, establishes prayer, pays zakat, and deals with people only with goodness."
"4601","The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You should accept Islam, then participate in the battle. The man accepted Islam, then participated in the battle and was martyred. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He did little deeds, but he will receive a great reward."
"4602","Leaving (for Jihad) in the way of Allah in the morning or in the evening (will merit a reward) better than the world and all that is in it. (Using translation from Muslim 1880)"
"4603","I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""Standing for a moment in the way of Allah is better than performing voluntary prayers at the Black Stone on the Night of Qadr."" (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) Mujahid heard specific hadiths from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him). Umar bin Darr also heard hadiths from him, and the person who thought that Mujahid did not hear any hadith from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) is mistaken, because Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) passed away in the fifty-eighth year of Hijrah during the caliphate of Sayyiduna Muawiyah (may Allah be pleased with him), while Mujahid was born in the twenty-first year of Hijrah during the caliphate of Sayyiduna Umar bin Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him), and Mujahid passed away in one hundred and three Hijri. So this indicates that Mujahid did hear from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him)."
"4604","The narrator says) Malik liked this statement very much. Malik moved ahead and went so far that his voice could still reach Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him). When he reached there, he called out loudly: O Abu Abdullah! Mount (your ride), Allah Almighty has granted you a mount. Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) realized why he had said this in a loud voice. He said: I have kept my mount in good condition, I do not need my people (I am walking on foot for this reason) because I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: “Whoever’s two feet become dusty in the way of Allah (while going for jihad), Allah makes the Hellfire forbidden for that person.” So all the people dismounted from their rides. The narrator says: We have never seen more people walking on foot than on that day. Maqri is a village near Damascus and Mahri is a quarter in Fustat. This was stated by the Sheikh."
"4605","The narrator named Sayyiduna Abu ‘Abs (may Allah be pleased with him) belonged to the people of Badr, whose name was ‘Abdur Rahman bin Jubair bin ‘Amr bin Zayd bin Jashm bin Harithah bin Harith bin Khazraj Al-Ansari. He passed away in 43 Hijri and was buried in Jannat al-Baqi’. Sayyiduna Abu Burdah bin Niyar (may Allah be pleased with him) and Sayyiduna Salamah bin Salamah bin Waqsh (may Allah be pleased with him) descended into his grave. In the narration of the people of Sham, the narrator named Walid will be Yazid bin Abu Maryam, and in the narration of the people of Iraq, it will be Burayd."
"4606","narrates this statement of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): ""Dust from the path of Allah and the smoke of Hell will never be together in the belly of any believing servant, and faith and envy cannot be together in the belly of any servant."
"4607","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The smoke of Hell and the dust in the way of Allah cannot be combined in the nostrils of any Muslim."
"4608","“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ slept near me one day, then he woke up smiling. I said: ‘O Messenger of Allah, what has made you smile?’ He said: ‘People of my nation who were shown to me (in my dream) riding across this sea like kings on thrones.’ I said: ‘Supplicate to Allah to make me one of them.’” So he prayed for her. Then he slept again, and did likewise, and she said the same as she said before, and he replied in the same manner. She said: “Pray to Allah to make me one of them,” and he said: “You will be one of the first ones.” He said: “Then she went out with her husband, ‘Ubadah bin Samit, as a fighter, the first time that the Muslims crossed the sea with Mu’awiyah bin Abu Sufyan. On their way back, after they had finished fighting, they stopped in Sham. An animal was brought near for her to ride it, but it threw her off, and she died.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 2776)"
"4609","The narrator named Abu Ma'n is Muhammad bin Ma'n Ghafari; he belonged to the people of Madinah, while the narrator named Abu Aqil is Zahrah bin Ma'bad, and he belonged to the people of Ramla. The name of Sayyiduna Uthman Ghani's (may Allah be pleased with him) servant Abu Salih is Harith."
"4610","Allah has undertaken to provide for one who leaves his home (only) to fight for His cause and to affirm the truth of His word; Allah will either admit him to Paradise or will bring him back home from where he had come out, with his reward and booty. (Using translation from Muslim 1876c)"
"4611","The distance between two of these levels is as great as the distance between the sky and the earth. So when you ask Allah Almighty, ask Him for Jannat al-Firdaws, for it is the middle and the highest level of Paradise, and above it is the Throne, and all the rivers of Paradise flow from it."" (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) The statement of the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that it is the middle level of Paradise means that Firdaws is in the middle of Paradise in terms of width. The statement of the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that it is the highest level of Paradise means that in terms of elevation (it is at the top)."
"4612","Abu Saʿid, whoever cheerfully accepts Allah as his Lord, Islam as his religion and Muhammad as his Apostle is necessarily entitled to enter Paradise. He (Abu Saʿid) wondered at it and said: Messenger of Allah, repeat it for me. He (the Messenger of Allah) did that and said: There is another act which elevates the position of a man in Paradise to a grade one hundred (higher), and the elevation between one grade and the other is equal to the height of the heaven from the earth. He (Abu Saʿid) said: What is that act? He replied: Jihad in the way of Allah! Jihad in the way of Allah! (Using translation from Muslim 1884)"
"4613","The one who participates in battle in the way of Allah, the one who performs Hajj to the House of Allah, and the one who performs Umrah are the guests of Allah. Allah Almighty has called them, and they come in response to His call."
"4614","I heard the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) say: “Whoever shoots one arrow in the way of Allah, it is like freeing a slave (in reward).”"
"4615","The narrator says: That day I shot sixteen arrows (i.e., that reached the enemy). Sheikh Abu Hatim states: The name of Sayyiduna Abu Yah (may Allah be pleased with him) is Amr bin Abasah Salmi."
"4616","The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is not like the threshold of your mother’s house, rather, between two ranks is a distance of one hundred years’ journey. (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) When the people said to Sayyiduna Ka’b bin Murrah (may Allah be pleased with him) that you narrate to us a hadith and be cautious, by this statement they meant that you should be careful not to make a mistake and not to narrate more or less words. They did not mean that you should be cautious of lying, because all the Companions are just (‘adil)—may Allah have mercy on them and grant us their company (in the Hereafter) as well."
"4617","Surely, the gates of Paradise are under the shadows of the swords. A man in a shabby condition got up and said; Abu Musa, did you hear the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say this? He said: Yes. (The narrator said): He returned to his friends and said: I greet you (a farewell greeting). Then he broke the sheath of his sword, threw it away, advanced with his (naked) sword towards the enemy and fought (them) with it until he was slain. (Using translation from Muslim 1902)"
"4618","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever fights for as long as it takes for a she-camel to be milked, Paradise becomes obligatory for such a person."
"4619","""I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'I am a Za'im - and the Za'im is the guarantor - for the one who believes in me and accepts Islam, and emigrates: A house on the outskirts of Paradise and a house in the middle of Paradise. And I am a guarantor, for the one who believes in me and accepts Islam, and strives in the cause of Allah: A house on the outskirts of Paradise and a house in the middle of Paradise and a house in the highest chambers of Paradise. Whoever does that and seeks goodness wherever it is, and avoids evil wherever it is, may die wherever he wants to die.'"" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 3133)"
"4620","narrator is unsure, perhaps these are the words:) Sayyiduna Muhammad (peace be upon him) said: Whoever is killed in the way of Allah (the narrator is unsure, perhaps these are the words), whoever dies in the way of Allah will be in Paradise."
"4621","The example of the one who strives in the path of Allah is like that of a fasting and praying person who does not leave off any (supererogatory) fast nor abandons (supererogatory) prayer until that person returns (from jihad)."
"4622","The example of one who strives in the path of Allah is like that of a person who performs voluntary prayers and fasts continuously, without any break in his prayer and fasting, until the warrior returns, bringing with him spoils and reward, or Allah causes him to die and admits him into Paradise."
"4623","Salman passed by ˹Shurahbil˺ while he was stationed for guarding and asked, ""What are you doing here, Shurahabil?"" Shurahabil replied, ""I am performing ribat (guarding) in the cause of Allah."" Salman said, ""I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, 'The act of guarding for a day or a night is better than fasting and praying for an entire month.'"""""
"4624","That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""The deeds of everyone who dies are sealed. Except for the one who dies guarding the frontier from the enemy, in the cause of Allah. For indeed his actions are increased for him until the Day of Judgement, and he is secure from the tribulation of the grave."" And I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying: ""The Mujahid is one who strives against his own soul."" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 1621)"
"4625","The narrator named Nu'man is Nu'man bin Mundhir Ghassani, and he belongs to the people of Damascus."
"4626","I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: Keeping watch for a day and a night is better (in point of reward) than fasting for a whole month and standing in prayer every night. If a person dies (while, performing this duty), his (meritorious) activity will continue and he will go on receiving his reward for it perpetually and will be saved from the torture of the grave. (Using translation from Muslim 1913a)"
"4627","The people said, ""O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)! Tell us of a deed that is equal to striving in the path of Allah."" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""You do not have the ability to do that."" The people said, ""O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)! Tell us, perhaps we may be able to do it."" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""The example of one who strives in the path of Allah is like that of a fasting person who stands (in prayer) reciting the verses of Allah, and he does not pause in his fasting or charity (and he continues to perform voluntary prayers and fasts) until the warrior returns to his home."
"4628","was narrated that ‘Umar bin al-Khattab ؓ said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever shades the head of a warrior, Allah will shade him on the Day of Resurrection; whoever equips a warrior until he is fully equipped, will have a reward like his; whoever builds a mosque in which the Name of Allah is mentioned. Allah will build for him a house in Paradise.” (Using translation from Aḥmad 376)"
"4629","Abu Sa’id Al Khudri said “The Apostle of Allaah ﷺ sent an expedition towards Banu Lihyan and said “One of the two persons should go forth. He then said to those who sat (at home), If any one of you looks after the family and property of a warrior, he will receive half the reward of the one who goes forth (in jihad).” (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 2510)"
"4630","“Whoever equips a warrior in the cause of Allah, he will have a reward like his, without that detracting from the warrior’s reward in the slightest.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 2759)"
"4631","Zaid bin Khalid al Juhani reported that Apostle of Allaah ﷺ as saying “He who equips a fighter in Allaah’s path has taken part in the fighting. And he looks after a fighter’s family when he is away has taken part in the fighting.” (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 2509)"
"4632","narrates this statement of the Noble Prophet : ""Whoever equips a warrior (mujahid) with supplies, he also receives a reward like that of the warrior. And whoever looks after the family of a warrior in his absence, he also receives a reward like that of the warrior."" Ibn Shihab states: Busar bin Sa'id narrated this hadith to me."
"4633","narrates this statement of the Noble Prophet : ""Whoever equips a person fighting in the way of Allah or looks after his family in his absence, he will also receive a reward like that of the fighter, but the reward of the fighter will not be diminished in any way. And if someone gives iftar to a fasting person, he will also receive a reward like that of the fasting person, and the reward of the fasting person will not be diminished in any way."
"4634","""The sanctity of the wives of the Mujahidin to those who stay behind is like the sanctity of their mothers. There is no man among those who stay behind who takes on the responsibility of looking after the wife of one of the Mujahidin (and betrays him) but he (the betrayer) will be made to stand before him on the Day Resurrection and it will be said: 'O So-and-so, this is so-and-so, take whatever you want from his good deeds.'"" Then the Prophet ﷺ turned to his Companions and said: ""What do you think: Will he leave him any of his good deeds?"" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 3191)"
"4635","The sanctity of the wives of the Mujahideen for those who stay behind is like the sanctity of their own mothers. And whoever among those who stay behind betrays a Mujahid regarding his wife, then on the Day of Resurrection, that person will be presented before the Mujahid and it will be said to the Mujahid: This person betrayed your wife in your absence, so take his good deeds."
"4636","A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, ""A man fights for pride and haughtiness another fights for bravery, and another fights for showing off; which of these (cases) is in Allah's Cause?"" The Prophet ﷺ said, ""The one who fights that Allah's Word (Islam) should be superior, fights in Allah's Cause."" (See Hadith No. 65, Vol. 4) (Using translation from Bukhārī 7458)"
"4637","A man said: Messenger of Allah, a man wishes to take part in jihad in Allah's path desiring some worldly advantage? The Prophet ﷺ said: He will have not reward. The people thought it terrible, and they said to the man: Go back to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, for you might not have made him understand well. He, therefore, (went and again) asked: Messenger of Allah, a man wishes to take part in jihad in Allah's path desiring some worldly advantage? He replied: There is no reward for him. They again said to the man: Return to the Messenger of Allah. He, therefore, said to him third time. He replied: There is no reward for him. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 2516)"
"4638","""Whoever fights seeking only an 'Iqal, then he will have what he intended."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 3139)"
"4639","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""That your horse's legs are cut and your blood is shed."
"4640","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “In that case, your horse’s legs will be cut and you will be martyred in the way of Allah.”"
"4641","I hope that all the gatekeepers of Paradise will call you."
"4642","I not honor you? Did I not make you a leader? Did I not get you married? Did I not subjugate horses and camels for you? Did I not bestow upon you all kinds of blessings? The servant will reply: Yes, my Lord (all this happened). The Lord will say: Did you believe that you would meet Me? He will reply: No, my Lord! So the Lord will say: Today I forget you just as you forgot Me. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Then another person will be presented, and the Lord will say: Did I not honor you? Did I not make you a leader? Did I not get you married? Did I not subjugate horses and camels for you? Did I not grant you abundance and prosperity? The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: That servant will reply: Yes, O my Lord! The Lord will ask: Did you believe that you would meet Me? The servant will reply: No, O my Lord! So the Lord will say: I forget you just as you forgot Me. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Then a third person will be presented, and the Lord will ask: Who are you? He will reply: I am Your servant, I believed in You, in Your Prophet, in Your Books, I fasted, I prayed, I gave charity, and he will mention all the good deeds he can. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: It will be said to this person: Did We not send a witness over you? The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: That person will think in his mind: Who can testify against me? The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Then a seal will be set upon his mouth, and it will be said to his thighs: Speak! So his thigh, his flesh, and his bones will speak about what he used to do. This will be a hypocrite person, so that he cannot present any excuse from his side, and so that Allah may express His anger upon him. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Then a caller will announce: Every group should follow what they used to worship. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: So those who worshipped the devils will go after the devils. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: The Jews and Christians will go with their leaders towards Hell. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Then only the believers will remain. O people of faith! Then we will remain, our Lord will come to us, He will be our Lord, He will say: For whom are you standing? The servants will reply: We are the servants who believe in Allah, we worship Him, He is our Lord, He will come to us and grant us reward, we are standing right here. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Then the Lord will say: I am your Lord, you may proceed. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Then the Bridge (Sirat) will be placed, upon which there will be hooks made of fire that will snatch people. At that place, permission for intercession will be granted (and I will supplicate): ""O Allah! Grant safety, O Allah! Grant safety."" When a person crosses this bridge, then everyone who gave a pair of anything from his wealth in the way of Allah, the gatekeepers of Paradise will call him: O servant of Allah, O Muslim, this is goodness. He will be told: O servant of Allah, O Muslim, this is goodness. Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) said: O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)! Will there be any harm to a person if he leaves one gate and enters from another? The narrator says: The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) struck his shoulder and said: ""By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, I hope you will be among those people."" The narrator named Abdul Jabbar says: The narrator named Sufyan dictated this narration to me."
"4643","The narrator says) I asked: What is meant by a pair of anything from wealth? He replied: That he frees two slaves from among his slaves, or gives two horses from among his horses, or gives two camels from among his camels."
"4644","The narrator says) I asked: What is meant by a pair? He replied: That he gives two horses from his horses, or two camels from his camels, or two slaves from his slaves. (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) In their idiom, the Arabs use the word “pair” for two similar things. Allah Almighty has also said: “And We have created pairs of everything.”"
"4645","Sayyiduna Abu Dharr Ghifari (may Allah be pleased with him). He had brought his camels (to the water) and was giving them water. Then he moved towards his mount; he had hung a water skin around the neck of his mount so that he could drink from it. He first gave water to his companions. This was included in the traditions of the Arabs. I said, “O Abu Dharr, what is your wealth?” He replied, “My wealth is my deeds.” I said, “O Abu Dharr, what did you hear the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) say?” He replied, “I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) say: ‘Whoever spends a pair from his wealth in the way of Allah, the gatekeepers of Paradise rush towards him.’” I asked, “O Abu Dharr, what is meant by a pair?” He replied, “If it is slaves, then two slaves; if it is horses, then two horses; if it is camels, then two camels (spent in the way of Allah),” until he counted all types of wealth. I said, “O Abu Dharr! (Please narrate) more (hadith).” So he said, “I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) say: ‘If three children of any two Muslims (i.e., a Muslim husband and wife) die, Allah, due to His mercy and grace upon those (children), will admit both of them (the husband and wife) into Paradise.’”"
"4646","“The best Dinar that a man can spend is a Dinar that he spends on his family, a Dinar that he spends on a horse in the cause of Allah, and a Dinar that a man spends on his companions in the cause of Allah.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 2760)"
"4647","narrates this statement of the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): ""Whoever spends anything in the way of Allah, its reward is recorded for him up to seven hundred times."
"4648","The example of those who spend their wealth in the way of Allah is like a grain of corn that grows seven ears, in every ear a hundred grains. And Allah multiplies for whom He wills, and Allah is All-Encompassing, All-Knowing."" the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) made this supplication: O my Lord! Grant my Ummah more. So Allah the Exalted revealed this verse: ""Who is it that will lend to Allah a goodly loan so He may multiply it for him many times over."" The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) supplicated: O my Lord! Grant my Ummah more. Then this verse was revealed: ""Indeed, the patient will be given their reward without account."
"4649","It is (offered) in the way of Allah. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: For this you will have seven hundred she-camels on the Day of Judgment all of which will be muzzled. (Using translation from Muslim 1892a)"
"4650","""On the Day of Resurrection seven hundred bridled camels will come to you."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 3187)"
"4651","Allah the Exalted and Great revealed (a verse) regarding those who were killed at Bi'r Ma'una, and we recited it, till it was abrogated later on (and the verse was like this):, convey to it our people the tidings that we have met our Lord, and He was pleased with us and we were pleased with Him"". (Using translation from Muslim 677a)"
"4652","One who is wounded in the way of Allah-and Allah knows better who is wounded in His way-will appear on the Day of Judgment with his wound bleediing. The colour (of its discharge) will be the colour of blood, (but) its smell will be the smell of musk. (Using translation from Muslim 1876d)"
"4653","""I heard Jabir say: 'A man said on the day of Uhud: If I am killed in the cause of Allah, where do you think I will be? He said: In Paradise. He threw down some dates that were in his hand and fought until he was killed.'"" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 3154)"
"4654","""A man came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: 'O Messenger of Allah, if I am killed in the cause of Allah with patience and seeking reward, facing the enemy and not running away, do you think that Allah will forgive my sins?' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Yes.' When the man turned away, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ called him back and said: 'What did you say?' He repeated his question, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Yes, except debt. Jibril told me.'"" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 3156)"
"4655","“The martyr does not feel anything more when he is killed than one of you feels if he is pinched (by a bug).” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 2802)"
"4656","The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Among the first three people to enter Paradise will be: a martyr, a slave who was loyal to his master and worshipped his Lord well, and a weak person who refrains from begging. And among the first three people to enter Hell will be: a tyrannical rich man, a wealthy person who does not fulfill Allah's right in his wealth, and an arrogant poor person."
"4657","“The believer’s soul is a bird that eats from the trees of Paradise, until it will be returned to his body on the Day when he is resurrected.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 4271)"
"4658","The martyrs will be at the bank of a river at the gate of Paradise, in a green dome. Their provision from Paradise will come to them morning and evening."
"4659","I was shown a dream. Two men came to me, they took hold of my hand and led me up a tree. They made me enter a house; I have never seen a house more beautiful than it. They told me: This is the abode of the martyrs."",""When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed the Fajr prayer"",""he would turn toward us with his face and say"","" 'Did anyone among you see a dream last night?' So"","" one day we asked him (about the dreams)"","" and he said"","" 'I saw two men coming to me and holding my hand"","" then they took me and ascended with me in a tree. They entered a house with me"","" which I had never seen anything better than. Then he said"","" 'This house is the house of martyrs'."""""""""
"4660","The martyr will intercede for seventy people from his household.”"
"4661","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""No person who enters Paradise will wish to return to the world, except for the martyr, because he will desire to return to the world and be martyred again."
"4662","Nobody who enters Paradise will (ever like to) return to this world even if he were offered everything on the surface of the earth (as an inducement) except the martyr who will desire to return to this world and be killed ten times for the sake of the great honour that has been bestowed upon him. (Using translation from Muslim 1877b)"
"4663","The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: There are three types of people who are killed. One is the person who is a believer, who participates in jihad in the way of Allah with his life and wealth, until when he faces the enemy, he fights and is martyred. He is the martyr who was put to trial; he will be under the Throne of Allah in a tent made by Allah, and only the rank of prophethood will be superior to him for the Prophets. The second is the person who is involved in sins and mistakes; he participates in jihad with his life and wealth, until when he faces the enemy, he fights and is martyred. This is the thing that wipes out his sins and mistakes; indeed, the sword wipes out sins. Such a person will enter Paradise through whichever of its eight doors he wishes. Paradise has eight doors, Hell has seven doors, and some of them are superior to others. And the third is the person who is a hypocrite, who participates in jihad with his life and wealth, until when he faces the enemy, he fights and is killed. This person will go to Hell, because the sword cannot wipe out hypocrisy."
"4664","The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Umm Haritha! Paradise has many levels, and Haritha is in the highest Firdaus."
"4665","narrates this statement of the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""A disbeliever and his killer will never be together in Hell."
"4666","narrates this statement of the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""Allah Almighty smiles at two men, one of whom has killed the other, and both of them will be in Paradise."" (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) This is the type of narration about which we have already stated in our books that the Arabs sometimes attribute certain actions to the one who commands them, just as they attribute actions to the one who performs them. Similarly, at times, they attribute something related to the actions of the creation to Allah Almighty, just as they attribute it to the creation. So, the statement of the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that Allah Almighty smiles at two men means: Allah Almighty tells the angels to laugh and commands them to rejoice regarding that disbeliever who had killed a Muslim, then Allah Almighty guides that disbeliever to the right path, he becomes a Muslim, and then by His grace, Allah grants him the rank of martyrdom, until both of them enter Paradise. So Allah Almighty amazes His angels at this and makes them laugh at this, which happens due to the presence of that which He has decreed and written in destiny. So here, the laughter that comes from the angels is attributed to Allah Almighty, which is in reference to His command and will. There are many more examples of this, which we will mention later in this book in the fifth section of the Sunan, if Allah Almighty so wills and decrees."
"4667","""The Messenger of Allah said: 'Allah will laugh at two persons- one of them kills the other, and both of them enter Paradise, for the first one fought in the cause of Allah and was martyred, then his killer repented to Allah and became Muslim, then he also fought in the cause of Allah and was martyred.'"" (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 191)"
"4668","narrates this statement of the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""Goodness has been placed in the forelocks of horses until the Day of Resurrection."
"4669","Great good is attached to the forelock of the horses until the Day of Judgment. (Using translation from Muslim 1873a)"
"4670","Messenger of Allah ﷺ ﷺ said, ""There is a blessing in the fore-heads of horses."" (Using translation from Bukhārī 2851)"
